  "notes": "Umm Al-Qura Cement Company (ticker 3005, a Saudi Joint Stock Company) audited financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2025 with FY2024 comparatives, from the full audited PDF in the 'Annual / 2025' cell of the Saudi Exchange company-profile 'Financial Statements' tab (Resources/fsPdf/602_0_2026-03-17...). Auditor: BDO Dr. Mohamed Al-Amri & Co. (Ahmed Fahad Al-Jumah, licence 621); unqualified opinion, dated Riyadh 15 March 2026. The financial statements were approved by the Board of Directors on 23 Ramadan 1447H (corresponding to 12 March 2026) - Note 27. Amounts are presented in full Saudi Riyals (scale 1) except per-share data. The auditor's report and the primary statements (printed FS pages 6-9) are scanned images in the filed PDF (transcribed from page renders at 2.6x); the notes are digital text. These are the Company's **standalone** (non-consolidated) statements - Umm Al-Qura Cement has no subsidiaries, hence no non-controlling interest. There are no discontinued operations - the standard pre-tax - zakat bridge applies (income_before_income_taxes_and_zakat is 'Net profit for the year before Zakat'). accounts_receivable is the combined 'Accounts receivable, prepaid expenses and other receivables' current-asset line; long_term_investments is 'Financial investments at fair value through OCI'; other_reserves is the 'Reserve for revaluation of financial investments at fair value through OCI'. long_term_debt / current_debt are the non-current and current portions of the 'Saudi Industrial Development Fund loan' - the whole remaining balance (SAR 200.1m) is classified as current at 31 December 2025, so no non-current fact is carried for FY2025; provisions is 'Provision for rehabilitation of areas subject to franchise license' (quarry / franchise-area restoration); defined_benefit_obligation is 'Employees' benefit liabilities'; accounts_payable is 'Accounts payable, accrued expenses and other payables'; zakat_payable is 'Zakat provision'; lease_liabilities_noncurrent / lease_liabilities_current are the reported lease-liability portions. On the P&L: other_income is 'Other income'; other_nonoperating_income is '(Loss) / Profits from foreign currency exchange' (a small net figure - a loss in FY2025, a gain in FY2024); other_nonoperating_expense is 'Losses on disposal of Property, plant and equipment'; finance_costs is 'Finance costs'; income_taxes_and_zakat is the 'Zakat' charge. On the cash-flow statement: depreciation_amortization combines PP&E depreciation, intangible-asset amortisation and right-of-use-asset depreciation; interest_paid is 'Finance costs paid'; zakat_paid is 'Zakat paid'; capex is 'Payment for purchase of property, plant and equipment'; debt_repaid is 'Repayment of Saudi Industrial Development Fund Loan'; lease_payments is 'Lease liabilities paid'; the cash-flow statement has no FX-on-cash line and its closing balance equals the balance-sheet 'Cash and cash equivalents' line exactly. **Softer year** - cost of sales rose faster than sales so gross margin eased from 31.2% to 27.6%, operating profit fell to SAR 60.2m and net profit to SAR 45.8m (EPS 0.83, FY2024 0.87). Statement page references are the printed FS page numbers: financial position 6, profit or loss and OCI 7, changes in equity 8, cash flows 9.",
